"limitations": ["Single shared development host; no CPU isolation or system cache flush.","Summarized steady phases start only after no direct GUI children for 1.2 seconds and 2 seconds extra settling.","Transient related processes between reads may be missed; observed peaks are lower bounds.","Zero helper memory means no helper observed in complete samples; missing reads remain incomplete.","Full comparison includes the renderer and management-page lifetime changes; no isolated attribution.","Synthetic 2000-world maximum-list scenario is not an ordinary user library or all-states memory bound.","Observer/controller and image capture are outside application and Xvfb process scopes.","All four GUI runs had observed SwapPss=0; host swap use remains reported separately.","The 160-character synthetic names deliberately exercise truncation; this is an upper-bound list-size business scenario, not a typical user's library.","Leaving Worlds did not visibly reduce steady resident memory within either binary; releasing Rust objects need not return allocator pages to the OS immediately.","Whole-operation Python and process-tree sampled peaks varied in direction, so this report does not establish a reduction in whole-operation peak memory.","Observed peaks may miss faster transients, especially when the candidate redraws more quickly. VmHWM is reported separately for the main process.","No FPS, interaction-latency, Windows-runtime, macOS-runtime, or all-states memory conclusion follows from this scenario."],
